    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d652">

                <pb facs="0715" n="707" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg707"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.6363/6157</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-09-19">September 19, 1939</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The British Ambassador called at his own request and handed me an <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi>,<anchor n="52" xml:id="d652-f1"/> a
                    copy of which is attached, in regard to the Mexican oil situation. I thanked him
                    for this information concerning the attitude of his Government toward the matter
                    and added that my Government was doing all it possibly could to aid in bringing
                    about a satisfactory settlement of the oil question.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ull</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d652-f1" n="52" xml:id="d652-f1-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Infra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
